## Editing these instructions

Keep each rule self-contained while linking the document that owns its rationale. Add a rule when its absence caused a real mistake, not when it is merely true. Condense when clarity survives; move detail to the owner document rather than letting this file grow. If a subtree needs its own orders, give that subtree its own `AGENTS.md` instead of adding a section here.
